- timestamp: '2026-11-08T09:30:25.502323+00:00'
  curator: Codex worker05 /root/buffer_tris
  action: WITHDRAW_UNSUPPORTED_COMPONENT_ID
  changes: The raw PY-fructose observation is Clostridium formicaceticum. Andreesen
    1970 publisher abstract confirms the organism and fructose metabolism but does
    not expose the recipe or digest. Full text is subscription-only in the captured
    free access. Later current culture media do not establish this historical PY formulation.
    The inherited peptone expansion remains interpreted and ungrounded. Withdraw the
    unsupported peptone component_id and set reference_scope UNMAPPED; retain its
    existing component_name as historical interpretation, not a newly observed expanded
    source label. The original assertion method and UNKNOWN/PARTIAL completeness remain
    unchanged. This is a bounded part-reference correction only. Whole-owner identity,
    raw labels, occurrence counts, quantities, unrelated components, all historical
    evidence and source/role/export holds are preserved. Historical all-components-identified
    statements describe prior states, not a new approval. No new MappingEvidence is
    added; historical human/component evidence enums are not rewritten. Filed before
    this private correction at https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1176#issuecomment-6719248666.
  previous_status: MAPPED
  new_status: MAPPED
  llm_assisted: true
  llm_model: gpt-6
